{"id": 18, "ts": 1779481415.6983023, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I\u2019d like to share a few observations from my interview that have not yet been discussed. Candidate\u202fC consistently puts crew welfare above all else and demonstrated excellent attention to detail, which strengthens his fit for crew\u2011cooperation and information\u2011accuracy criteria. However, I have no direct evidence of his calmness or effectiveness under pressure, which remains an open question. For Candidate\u202fA, I have no observations on stress resilience either, but I noted that he is unfriendly and has unhealthy eating habits, raising minor concerns for team dynamics and personal health. Candidate\u202fB was perceived as pretentious and sometimes uses an inappropriate tone, which could undermine professional communication despite his strong stress handling. Candidate\u202fD appears moody and is regarded as a loner, suggesting possible challenges for crew interaction, though he shows strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility. Given the current evidence, I remain provisionally inclined toward Candidate\u202fC, provided we can address his communication gaps, but we should seek additional data on calmness under pressure for Candidates\u202fA,\u202fC, and\u202fD.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
